          "text": "Left lower leg ulcer"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 3 x 4 cm shallow ulcer at the medial gaiter; irregular sloping edges, granulation tissue and some yellow slough. Moderate serous ooze. Mild erythema and warmth limited to a 0.5–1 cm rim; no clear spreading cellulitis, crepitus, necrosis, or foul smell."
      }
